I was originally planning to write a six-month reflection about my time at Scotiabank, but time really flew by—and somehow, I’m already at the seven-and-a-half-month mark.

So, why Scotiabank?

When I first arrived in Canada in 2022, one of the first things I did the next morning was head to the nearest Scotiabank branch to open an account. It was a small but important step that helped me start settling into a new country and building my life here.

So, when I received the opportunity to join Scotiabank, I didn’t hesitate. I was excited to move from Montreal to Toronto—where my French wouldn’t be put to the test quite as often—and contribute to a company that had supported me when I was first getting settled in Canada.

Over the past seven and a half months, I’ve learned a lot while working with an incredible team. I’ve had the chance to learn about and contribute to microfrontend architecture on the frontend, work with AI on the backend, and lead a group of interns who brought thoughtful and innovative ideas to the products they worked on.

Beyond the technical growth, I’ve really appreciated the chance to connect with the team outside of work. Whether through team events or volunteering, those moments have brought us closer together and made work even more enjoyable.

I also volunteered at a food bank for the first time, where the time flew by and I picked up an unexpected new skill: the interlocking flap technique!

Most of all, I’m grateful to be part of a team that has grown from five people when I joined to eighteen today. It has been exciting to see that growth firsthand and to be surrounded by people who have supported me from day one.

Looking forward to what’s next!
